      "test_unicode_escape_validation.py": {
        "kind": "intent_a",
        "rationale": "Change A rejects \\u/\\U escapes whose digits are not pure hex. Change B moves single-line string bodies onto a bulk-scan fast path, so the ordinary text around an escape is consumed differently. These tests embed malformed escapes between long runs of ordinary characters in single-line basic strings, which is B's fast path. They also cover quoted keys, table headers, inline tables and arrays, which all go through the rewritten _parse_string. Rejection must still happen on the merged tree. Base and B-only accept these inputs."
      },
      "test_string_scan_escapes.py": {
        "kind": "invariant",
        "rationale": "Every tree must keep three behaviours. First, valid \\u/\\U escapes surrounded by long ordinary runs decode to the right characters and the document round-trips byte-for-byte. Second, literal strings containing an escape-like sequence stay raw. Third, the error types after an escape are unchanged: a control character raises InvalidControlChar and a missing closing quote raises UnexpectedEofError. A changes how escape digits are validated, B changes how the text after an escape is scanned, and their combination must not regress any of this."
      }
    }
  },
